    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15456" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕlĕphantīne</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλεφαντίνη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small but very fertile island of the Nile</i>,
				<i>in the Thebaid</i>, <i>with a city
				of the same name</i>, now <i>Jezyret-Assuan</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Mel.
				1, 9, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 7, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 2,
			61</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 24, 17, 102, §
			163</span></i>.—Also called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Elĕphantis</span></b> , ĭdis,
				f., <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 9, 10, § 59</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Vitr.
				8, 2, 6</span></i>.</div>
